    "description": "NixOS Package PRs for kmod, gnugrep, zstd-1.5.5, xz-5.4.3, bzip2-1.0.8, gzip packages on GitHub",
    "items": [
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44400303?u=55a8f2cae9a85a082e32206e93cc3430039d26ec&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">The primary motivation for this PR is that I wanted a microVM with a <code class=\"notranslate\">tinyconfig</code> kernel and it doesn't set <code class=\"notranslate\">CONFIG_MODULES</code> (i.e. <code class=\"notranslate\">CONFIG_MODULES</code> is then set to <code class=\"notranslate\">=n</code>, which is ideal for my use-case).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Up until now, the Linux kernel build infrastructure always assumed <code class=\"notranslate\">CONFIG_MODULES=y</code> (introduced in <a class=\"commit-link\" data-hovercard-type=\"commit\" data-hovercard-url=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/commit/f95d214cfdf115b9444acc5ce8060a5b1b23ed77/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/commit/f95d214cfdf115b9444acc5ce8060a5b1b23ed77\"><tt>f95d214</tt></a> (\"Implement generic kernel build via manual-config\")). This PR basically allows building with <code class=\"notranslate\">CONFIG_MODULES=n</code>.</p>\n<h2 dir=\"auto\">Things done</h2>\n\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> Fits <a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md\">CONTRIBUTING.md</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/pkgs/README.md\">pkgs/README.md</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/maintainers/README.md\">maintainers/README.md</a> and other READMEs.</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> Follows the <a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/CONTRIBUTING.md#automationai-policy\">automation/AI policy</a>.</li>\n<li>Built on platform:\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> x86_64-linux</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> aarch64-linux</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> aarch64-darwin</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Tested, as applicable:\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> Basic functionality of all binary files, usually in <code class=\"notranslate\">./result/bin/</code>.</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> Ran <code class=\"notranslate\">nixpkgs-review</code> on this PR. See <a href=\"https://github.com/Mic92/nixpkgs-review#usage\">nixpkgs-review usage</a>.</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> <a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/pkgs/README.md#package-tests\">Package tests</a> at <code class=\"notranslate\">passthru.tests</code>.</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> <a href=\"https://nixos.org/manual/nixos/unstable/index.html#sec-nixos-tests\" rel=\"nofollow\">NixOS tests</a> in <a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/nixos/tests\">nixos/tests</a>.</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> Tests in <a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/lib/tests\">lib/tests</a> or <a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/pkgs/test\">pkgs/test</a> for functions and \"core\" functionality.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/doc/release-notes\">Nixpkgs Release Notes</a>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> Package update: when the change is major or breaking.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/NixOS/nixpkgs/blob/master/nixos/doc/manual/release-notes\">NixOS Release Notes</a>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> Module addition: when adding a new NixOS module.</li>\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Incomplete task\"> Module update: when the change is significant.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>",
